-- title:
--   Absorbing iteration of actual trace returns
-- statement:
--   Fix a ground size $n$, natural rank parameter $r$, Boolean subset oracles, a tape, an annealing schedule $s$, rational activity $q$, and multiplier table $w$. For a list $\ell$ of natural numbers and an initial optional restart cursor $u$, the trace fold repeatedly applies the actual capped trace-return operation, preserving failure:
--   $$
--   F([],u)=u,\qquad
--   F(k::\ell,u)=F(\ell,T(u)),\qquad
--   T(\operatorname{none})=\operatorname{none},\quad
--   T(\operatorname{some}(v))=\operatorname{traceReturn}(v).\mathrm{val}.
--   $$
--   The natural entries $k$ are ignored, so only their number matters. The definition projects the value from the charged fold and does not renormalize failed executions or assert that a return succeeds.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/CappedTraceIterationSubkernel.lean#L15-L22

